## Why This Is Asked
This tests event-driven reasoning, idempotent cross-region replication, and minimal IAM in GCP.

## Key Concepts
- Cloud Functions trigger on Cloud Storage finalize events
- Copy between buckets across regions, preserving path
- Idempotency via MD5 hash comparison
- Least privilege IAM and retry semantics
- Basic test plan including re-upload scenario

## Code Example
```javascript
const {Storage} = require('@google-cloud/storage');
const storage = new Storage();
const SRC = 'ingest-bucket';
const DST = 'dr-bucket';
exports.replicateToDR = async (event, context) => {
  const file = event.name;
  const srcFile = storage.bucket(SRC).file(file);
  // get MD5 from metadata
  const [md] = await srcFile.getMetadata().then(m => [m.md5Hash]);
  const dstFile = storage.bucket(DST).file(file);
  try {
    const [dstMeta] = await dstFile.getMetadata().catch(() => [null]);
    if (dstMeta && dstMeta.md5Hash === md) { return; }
    await srcFile.copy(dstFile);
  } catch (e) {
    // publish to Pub/Sub/log for alerting
    throw e;
  }
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you scale this for large files or many concurrent events?
- How would you monitor, alert, and test failure scenarios?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests multi-tenant isolation, streaming ETL, and observability under scale. 

## Key Concepts
- Pub/Sub isolation per-tenant; 
- Dataflow streaming autoscaling; 
- Beam schema normalization; 
- Tenant-scoped BigQuery with day partition; 
- IAM/service accounts and least privilege; 
- exactly-once semantics and dead-letter handling.

## Code Example
```java
// PTransform sketch: normalize, enrich, and write to BigQuery per-tenant
PCollection<Event> raw = p.apply("Read", PubsubIO.readStrings().fromTopic(tenantTopic));
PCollection<Event> normalized = raw.apply("Normalize", ParDo.of(new NormalizeFn()));
PCollection<Event> enriched = normalized.apply("Enrich", ParDo.of(new EnrichFn(tenantMetadata)));
enriched.apply("WriteBQ", BigQueryIO.<Event>write()
  .to("project:dataset.${tenant}.events$")
  .partitioning("DAY")
  .withSchema(Event.getSchema())
  .withWriteDisposition(WriteDisposition.WRITE_APPEND));
```

